description:
[narrowed from route-edit-d3b7c5e0] In repos/goal-host-vessel/src/index.ts, raise the evidence bar of the landedShaForGoalHash helper so it cannot grade a partial or wrong landing as reached, and correct a doc comment that states an invariant the code does not hold.

Background. The helper currently proves only that A COMMIT EXISTS carrying the goal hash. Measured 2026-09-03: dispatch b64c330f landed commit 023f9b1 for route-edit-c10beb80, the goal was "make a duplicated sentence appear exactly once", the sentence still appears twice, and the helper graded reached:true — a false positive. The doc comment says the check cannot manufacture a green the existing rule would refuse; for that dispatch the existing rule (a FAVORABLE compose report carrying a cutover new_git_sha) WOULD have refused, and the helper graded true anyway.

The comment also explains why the weaker bar was chosen: a retried compose OVERWROTE the report after a successful landing, so the report could not be trusted. That is no longer true. development-vessel commit ce10c8b now preserves a FAVORABLE report carrying a landed sha and writes the failed retry to a sibling file instead. The premise that justified the weaker bar is obsolete.

EDIT A. Find this exact single line:

 * caller's verdict untouched. Strictly false-negative → true-positive, never the reverse.

Replace it with these lines:

 * caller's verdict untouched.
 *
 * A COMMIT IS NOT AN ACHIEVEMENT. A sha carrying the goal hash proves work landed; it does
 * not prove the work did what the goal asked. Measured 2026-09-03: dispatch b64c330f landed
 * 023f9b1 for route-edit-c10beb80 and the goal was not met, and grading that reached:true
 * was a false positive produced by this helper. So the sha is necessary and not sufficient:
 * the report gate below demands the same evidence the :15968 reconciler demands. The report
 * is trustworthy again because ce10c8b stopped a failed retry from overwriting a FAVORABLE
 * one. Every failure path still returns null and leaves the caller's verdict untouched.

EDIT B. Find this exact single line:

    return /^[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test(out) ? out : null;

Replace it with:

    if (!/^[0-9a-f]{40}$/.test(out)) return null;
    // Necessary, not sufficient. Demand the compose report agree: FAVORABLE verdict and a
    // cutover carrying a new_git_sha — the exact bar the reconciler at :15968 applies, which
    // refuses staged-not-landed on the grounds that grading it "manufactures a hollow green".
    // Any doubt (missing, unreadable, unfavorable, no landed sha) returns null, so this can
    // only ever WITHHOLD a reach, never invent one.
    try {
      const reportFile = Bun.file(`/workspace/proposals/route-edit-${h}-compose-report.json`);
      if (!(await reportFile.exists())) return null;
      const report = JSON.parse(await reportFile.text()) as Record<string, unknown>;
      if (report.verdict !== "FAVORABLE") return null;
      const cutovers = Array.isArray(report.cutovers) ? (report.cutovers as Array<Record<string, unknown>>) : [];
      const landed = cutovers.some((c) => {
        const res = (c?.result ?? {}) as Record<string, unknown>;
        return typeof res.new_git_sha === "string" && res.new_git_sha.length > 0;
      });
      if (!landed) return null;
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
    return out;

Do not modify any other function. In particular do not touch the recordGoalPath function that follows this one. Change only this one file.

